    "https://www.yhc.edu/careers/#assistant-professor-of-theatre": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Theatre",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Theatre. Description Assistant Professor of Theatre The Young Harris College Department of Theatre invites applications for a full-time tenure tracked Assistant Professor of Theatre for an appointment beginning August 2027. This position’s primary responsibilities will be to teach courses in musical theatre and theatre, and direct in the mainstage season. The position is based in the city of Young Harris, which is in the beautiful Appalachian Mountains of North Georgia. The successful candidate must hold a terminal degree in acting or a closely related field and be capable of teaching acting at all levels, as well as related support courses, and directing up to two productions per academic year. The ideal applicant will be a creative collaborator with significant professional experience in musical theatre and a background in higher education. Ability to teach in related areas — including but not limited to movement, voice and diction, song as monologue, audition techniques, and professional readiness — is highly desirable. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis beginning October 1 and continuing through the fall semester; candidates are encouraged to apply promptly. Theatre Young Harris is a highly successful program offering three degrees: a B.F.A. in Musical Theatre, a B.A. in Theatre Performance, and a B.A. in Theatrical Design and Production. The department maintains between 30–45 majors across these degrees, and also offers a minor in Theatre, a minor in Dance, and a new B.S. in Arts Administration. For more than a decade, most of our students have attained paid jobs, paid internships, or fully-funded graduate school in theatre within 12 months of graduation. As a department, we produce four mainstage productions per year (two musicals and two plays), as well as an additional 4–6 shows in our Second Season and Studio Series. Apply Now About Young Harris College Young Harris College is proud of its Wesleyan heritage and commitment. The College was founded by a Methodist circuit-rider, and its namesake and sustainer during the institution’s formative years was one of the state’s outstanding Methodist laypeople. For several years, all Presidents of the College were ordained Methodist ministers, with Young Harris later appointing professional educators who were active lay leaders in the Methodist Church to the presidency. Today, Young Harris is a member of the North American Association of Methodist Schools, Colleges, and Universities (NAAMSCU), a voluntary association of over 100 private schools, colleges, universities, and seminaries in the United States that cooperate to advance the common good of member institutions and to address issues of mutual concern to the church and the academy. Young Harris is also a member of the University Senate of the UMC’s General Board of Higher Education and Ministry (GBHEM), making the institution eligible for funding from UMC agencies. Young Harris supports the UMC’s commitment to “open hearts, open minds, and open doors.” For more information about the College’s affiliation with GBEHM, follow this link: GBHEM . Young Harris College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex , age, disability, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. EOE M/F/D/V local laws. Young Harris College is committed to providing an inclusive and accessible application process for all applicants. If you need a reasonable accommodation at any point during the application or hiring process, we encourage you to contact Human Resources at hr@yhc.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.yhc.edu/careers/#adjunct-instructor-of-theatre": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Theatre",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Theatre. Description Adjunct Instructor of Theatre The Young Harris College Department of Theatre invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Theatre for spring 2027. This position’s primary responsibilities will be to teach courses in musical theatre and theatre, and potentially direct in the mainstage season. The college is based in the city of Young Harris, which is in the beautiful Appalachian Mountains of North Georgia. The successful candidate must hold a terminal degree in theatre or a closely related field and be capable of teaching acting courses and support courses. The ideal applicant will be a creative collaborator with significant professional experience in theatre in addition to experience in higher education. The ability to teach in related areas is also highly desirable. These possible areas include but are not limited to the following: acting, acting for musical theatre, voice and diction, theatre history, and audition techniques. Applications are accepted on an ongoing basis and reviewed as received. Candidates are encouraged to apply promptly. Theatre Young Harris is a highly successful program offering three degrees: a B.F.A. in Musical Theatre, a B.A. in Theatre Performance, and a B.A. in Theatrical Design and Production. The department maintains between 30-45 majors in these degrees, as well as offering a minor in Theatre, a minor in Dance, and a new B.S. in Arts Administration. For more than a decade, most of our students have attained paid jobs, paid internships, or fully-funded graduate school in theatre within 12 months of graduation. As a department we produce 4 mainstage productions per year (two musicals and two plays) as well as an additional 4-6 shows in our Second Season and Studio Series. Apply Now About Young Harris College Young Harris College is proud of its Wesleyan heritage and commitment. The College was founded by a Methodist circuit-rider, and its namesake and sustainer during the institution’s formative years was one of the state’s outstanding Methodist laypeople. For several years, all Presidents of the College were ordained Methodist ministers, with Young Harris later appointing professional educators who were active lay leaders in the Methodist Church to the presidency. Today, Young Harris is a member of the North American Association of Methodist Schools, Colleges, and Universities (NAAMSCU), a voluntary association of over 100 private schools, colleges, universities, and seminaries in the United States that cooperate to advance the common good of member institutions and to address issues of mutual concern to the church and the academy. Young Harris is also a member of the University Senate of the UMC’s General Board of Higher Education and Ministry (GBHEM), making the institution eligible for funding from UMC agencies. Young Harris supports the UMC’s commitment to “open hearts, open minds, and open doors.” For more information about the College’s affiliation with GBEHM, follow this link: GBHEM . Young Harris College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex , age, disability, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. EOE M/F/D/V local laws. Young Harris College is committed to providing an inclusive and accessible application process for all applicants. If you need a reasonable accommodation at any point during the application or hiring process, we encourage you to contact Human Resources at hr@yhc.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.yhc.edu/careers/#instructional-designer": {
      "title": "Instructional Designer",
      "description": "Instructional Designer. Job Title: Instructional Designer Reports to: Dean of Dual Enrollment & Distance Learning Summary: The Instructional Designer, an on-campus and in-person position, leads the design, development, and continuous improvement of classroom, online, and hybrid courses and programs. This position partners closely with faculty to enhance teaching effectiveness through the integration of sound pedagogical practices and instructional technologies that support student engagement and learning outcomes. The position supports institutional goals related to quality assurance, academic integrity, accessibility, and innovation in digital learning Serving as the primary resource for the institution’s learning management system (LMS), the Instructional Designer provides both strategic oversight and day-to-day support for online course delivery. The role collaborates extensively with academic leadership and the Office of Information Technology to ensure the effective implementation and support of instructional technologies aligned with the college’s academic mission. Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following. Other duties may be assigned. · Collaborate with faculty to design, develop, and revise classroom, online, and hybrid course materials, aligning pedagogical objectives with appropriate instructional technologies · Coordinate the proposal, development, review, and evaluation of online courses, and support decision-making related to online course offerings in collaboration with the Dean of Dual Enrollment & Distance Learning · Plan and deliver individual and group training for faculty on instructional technologies and effective teaching methodologies, in collaboration with academic leadership · Serve as the primary resource for faculty on the use of the LMS and other digital tools to support the delivery of course content · Develop and maintain online training materials and resources to support faculty use of educational technologies · Research, evaluate, and recommend emerging instructional technologies, including artificial intelligence (AI), to enhance course design, delivery, and support · Collaborate with the Office of Information Technology to ensure the reliability, functionality, and effectiveness of the LMS and other instructional systems Education and/or Experience: · Bachelor’s degree in instructional design, educational technology, curriculum and instruction, or a related field is required. · Master’s degree is preferred. · Demonstrated experience designing and developing online, in-person, or hybrid courses within a higher education environment is required. · Strong knowledge of instructional design frameworks, learning theory, and effective online pedagogy is required. · Experience applying accessibility standards and Universal Design for Learning (UDL) principles in digital course design is required. · Exceptional interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, with the ability to consult effectively across disciplines and organizational levels is required. · Proficiency with learning management systems and related instructional technologies is required. Moodle experience is strongly preferred. · Demonstrated success partnering with faculty and academic leadership to advance institutional goals for teaching and learning is preferred. · Familiarity with Quality Matters or other recognized quality assurance frameworks for online learning is preferred. · Commitment to and experience with ensuring academic integrity through technologies and course design. Apply Now About Young Harris College Young Harris College is proud of its Wesleyan heritage and commitment. The College was founded by a Methodist circuit-rider, and its namesake and sustainer during the institution’s formative years was one of the state’s outstanding Methodist laypeople. For several years, all Presidents of the College were ordained Methodist ministers, with Young Harris later appointing professional educators who were active lay leaders in the Methodist Church to the presidency. Today, Young Harris is a member of the North American Association of Methodist Schools, Colleges, and Universities (NAAMSCU), a voluntary association of over 100 private schools, colleges, universities, and seminaries in the United States that cooperate to advance the common good of member institutions and to address issues of mutual concern to the church and the academy. Young Harris is also a member of the University Senate of the UMC’s General Board of Higher Education and Ministry (GBHEM), making the institution eligible for funding from UMC agencies. Young Harris supports the UMC’s commitment to “open hearts, open minds, and open doors.” For more information about the College’s affiliation with GBEHM, follow this link: GBHEM . Young Harris College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex , age, disability, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. EOE M/F/D/V local laws. Young Harris College is committed to providing an inclusive and accessible application process for all applicants. If you need a reasonable accommodation at any point during the application or hiring process, we encourage you to contact Human Resources at hr@yhc.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.yhc.edu/careers/#director-of-cross-country-and-track-field": {
      "title": "Director of Cross Country and Track & Field",
      "description": "Director of Cross Country and Track & Field. Description Director of Cross Country and Track and Field Young Harris College | Young Harris, Georgia Young Harris College invites applications for the position of Director of Cross Country and Track and Field. The Director will provide comprehensive leadership for the College’s cross country and track and field programs, overseeing all aspects of coaching, recruiting, student-athlete development, team administration, and program advancement. Competing in Conference Carolinas and NCAA Division II, Young Harris College is committed to providing a holistic student-athlete experience that supports academic achievement, personal growth, athletic excellence, and meaningful engagement with the campus and broader community. The successful candidate will be an effective coach and mentor who builds a positive, inclusive, and competitive team culture while ensuring compliance with all College, Conference Carolinas, and NCAA Division II policies, rules, and regulations. The Director will also contribute to community outreach and fundraising initiatives and collaborate with colleagues across campus to advance the mission and visibility of the program. Primary Responsibilities Lead all aspects of the cross country and track and field programs, including practice planning, competition preparation, coaching, and student-athlete development. Recruit, evaluate, and retain qualified student-athletes who align with the academic and athletic mission of Young Harris College. Develop individualized training and development plans that support student-athletes’ athletic growth and competitive success. Foster a positive, disciplined, and team-oriented culture built on accountability, respect, sportsmanship, and personal development. Promote high academic achievement by establishing appropriate academic expectations and supporting student-athletes through study halls, academic meetings, and other resources. Coordinate team logistics, scheduling, travel, competition preparation, equipment, and other administrative responsibilities. Conduct and coordinate scouting, film review, performance analysis, and other preparation necessary for successful competition. Maintain effective communication and professional relationships with student-athletes, coaches, administrators, faculty, staff, alumni, and community partners. Support community outreach, fundraising, alumni engagement, and other initiatives that promote and strengthen the program. Ensure the program operates in full compliance with Young Harris College, Conference Carolinas, and NCAA Division II rules and regulations. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the College and the Department of Athletics. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Collegiate coaching or competitive collegiate playing experience required. Demonstrated ability to recruit, mentor, develop, and motivate student-athletes. Strong interpersonal, organizational, communication, and leadership skills. Commitment to the academic, athletic, and personal development of student-athletes. Demonstrated commitment to NCAA Division II rules and regulations and the values of Young Harris College. Ability and willingness to work a flexible schedule, including early mornings, evenings, weekends, and travel as required. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to: Build strong, professional relationships with student-athletes, coaches, administrators, faculty, staff, alumni, and community members. Communicate effectively with student-athletes and members of the coaching and administrative staffs. Lead a team in a manner that promotes accountability, collaboration, discipline, sportsmanship, and a positive student-athlete experience. Manage multiple priorities and administrative responsibilities while maintaining attention to detail. Recruit and retain student-athletes who contribute to the academic and competitive goals of the program. Work collaboratively across campus and represent Young Harris College positively within the community. Adapt to changing priorities and the demands of a collegiate athletics environment. Apply Now About Young Harris College Young Harris College is proud of its Wesleyan heritage and commitment. The College was founded by a Methodist circuit-rider, and its namesake and sustainer during the institution’s formative years was one of the state’s outstanding Methodist laypeople. For several years, all Presidents of the College were ordained Methodist ministers, with Young Harris later appointing professional educators who were active lay leaders in the Methodist Church to the presidency. Today, Young Harris is a member of the North American Association of Methodist Schools, Colleges, and Universities (NAAMSCU), a voluntary association of over 100 private schools, colleges, universities, and seminaries in the United States that cooperate to advance the common good of member institutions and to address issues of mutual concern to the church and the academy. Young Harris is also a member of the University Senate of the UMC’s General Board of Higher Education and Ministry (GBHEM), making the institution eligible for funding from UMC agencies. Young Harris supports the UMC’s commitment to “open hearts, open minds, and open doors.” For more information about the College’s affiliation with GBEHM, follow this link: GBHEM . Young Harris College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex , age, disability, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. EOE M/F/D/V local laws. Young Harris College is committed to providing an inclusive and accessible application process for all applicants. If you need a reasonable accommodation at any point during the application or hiring process, we encourage you to contact Human Resources at hr@yhc.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.yhc.edu/careers/#assistant-women-s-lacrosse-coach": {
      "title": "Assistant Women’s Lacrosse Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Women’s Lacrosse Coach. Description The Full-Time Assistant Women’s Lacrosse Coach at Young Harris College will assist the head coach in all aspects of the program, including on-field coaching, recruiting qualified student-athletes, player development, and team administrative responsibilities. Competing in Conference Carolinas and NCAA Division II, Young Harris values and emphasizes a holistic experience for student-athletes, requiring an assistant coach who can be a mentor, foster a positive team culture, and ensure compliance with all College and NCAA DII regulations. This position also involves engaging in community outreach, assisting with fundraising efforts, and collaborating with individuals across campus. Primary Responsibilities: Assist with practice planning, scouting reports, and player development. Coordinate a specific area of the field (offense or defense) at a high level. Recruit qualified student-athletes. Work closely with student-athletes to develop individual and team lacrosse skills. Promote high academic achievement within the program through team study halls and academic meetings. Support and organize team logistics, scheduling, film breakdown, and travel coordination. Foster a disciplined team culture. Qualifications Collegiate playing or coaching experience required. Bachelor’s degree required. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Candidates must exhibit the ability to build professional relationships with student-athletes and other staff members. Strong communication with the coaching staff and team are essential. They must demonstrate a commitment to adhere to Young Harris College, Conference Carolinas, and NCAA DII rules and regulations. Candidates must be flexible to work early mornings, evenings, and weekends. Apply Now About Young Harris College Young Harris College is proud of its Wesleyan heritage and commitment. The College was founded by a Methodist circuit-rider, and its namesake and sustainer during the institution’s formative years was one of the state’s outstanding Methodist laypeople. For several years, all Presidents of the College were ordained Methodist ministers, with Young Harris later appointing professional educators who were active lay leaders in the Methodist Church to the presidency. Today, Young Harris is a member of the North American Association of Methodist Schools, Colleges, and Universities (NAAMSCU), a voluntary association of over 100 private schools, colleges, universities, and seminaries in the United States that cooperate to advance the common good of member institutions and to address issues of mutual concern to the church and the academy. Young Harris is also a member of the University Senate of the UMC’s General Board of Higher Education and Ministry (GBHEM), making the institution eligible for funding from UMC agencies. Young Harris supports the UMC’s commitment to “open hearts, open minds, and open doors.” For more information about the College’s affiliation with GBEHM, follow this link: GBHEM . Young Harris College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex , age, disability, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. EOE M/F/D/V local laws. Young Harris College is committed to providing an inclusive and accessible application process for all applicants. If you need a reasonable accommodation at any point during the application or hiring process, we encourage you to contact Human Resources at hr@yhc.edu ."
    }
